## Independent method and falsifiable criteria

`SCOPE.md` froze the criteria before the audit implementation. The standalone
`audit_actual_candidate.py` imports no integration helper, native queue code
or root inspection predicate. It parses the concrete JSON and CSV data,
compares complete dictionaries and rows, scans physical CR/LF CSV record
boundaries independently, hashes every offered and captured body, checks real
process records against the immutable settings, and challenges the independent
predicates with mutations. JSON comparisons distinguish type differences by
canonical serialization; the checks use explicit exceptions and continue to
operate under Python optimization.

The final identical audit source passed twice:

- Normal mode: actual PID 70473, exit 0, 52,385 checks, 631 input read pins.
- Optimized mode: actual PID 70935, exit 0, 52,385 checks, 631 input read pins.
- Each mode detected all 13 independent negative controls: unrelated
  assessment and state modifications, changed rank, reordered catalog rows,
  reset target turns, changed CSV header and unrelated CSV body, changed CPU,
  file-size and open-file control policies, returned applied-limit mismatch,
  substituted execution SHA, and substituted worker PID.

The separate execution folders retain actual argv, clean environment, PID,
UTC start/end, exit, reaping, exact source SHA and complete small stdout and
stderr bodies. Six bounded, read-only local Git processes per successful mode
independently retrieve the three sparse-absent small baseline files and check
current main, branch and empty index. They retain at most 4,096-byte prefixes,
full byte counts and SHAs; they do not duplicate full large baseline buffers.
The live nine materialized native baseline bodies remained unchanged before
and after review.

